WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.167
Data leakage happens when the model receives information during training that would not truly be available when making a

00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:08.532
future prediction.

00:00:08.532 --> 00:00:15.217
A direct example would be accidentally including the target itself—or a variable derived from the future answer—inside

00:00:15.217 --> 00:00:16.668
the feature set.

00:00:17.207 --> 00:00:21.149
Leakage can make evaluation look unrealistically strong.

00:00:21.149 --> 00:00:27.054
Split data before final evaluation, keep target information out of the features,

00:00:27.054 --> 00:00:33.934
and make sure cleaning steps are applied consistently without using test information improperly.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:40.542
A model is only useful if its evaluation resembles the conditions in which it will actually be used.
